Problem:
	In 4.4.2, uart_poll_out() returns as soon as a byte is in the LPUART TX
	FIFO, not after it has been transmitted. mcux_lpuart_configure() then
	calls LPUART_Init(), which software-resets the peripheral and discards
	any bytes still in the FIFO.

	On the DEV-G2-NANO, this breaks Bluetooth bring-up. The NXP Bluetooth
	setup driver (hci_nxp_setup.c) sends the final firmware-download ACK with
	uart_poll_out() and immediately reconfigures the UART. The ACK is lost,
	the IW416 stays in its ROM bootloader, and bt init fails with a 0xFC09
	or 0x0C03 command timeout.

Fix:
	This issue was addressed in the following upstream Zephyr commits:
		1. 1aac1518d1ca6cbc5786f7e1c25174c23552fdb7
		2. c5469546d603d80f99935ea8416bff903a152007

	This patch just applies the diff.

--- a/drivers/serial/uart_mcux_lpuart.c
+++ b/drivers/serial/uart_mcux_lpuart.c
@@ -1367,6 +1367,11 @@
 {
 	const struct mcux_lpuart_config *config = dev->config;

+	if (!WAIT_FOR((config->base->STAT & LPUART_STAT_TC_MASK) != 0U,
+		      300U * USEC_PER_MSEC, k_busy_wait(100U))) {
+		return -EBUSY;
+	}
+
 	/* Disable Transmitter and Receiver */
 	config->base->CTRL &= ~(LPUART_CTRL_TE_MASK | LPUART_CTRL_RE_MASK);

